{"type": "message", "message": "**Warm white** is white with a subtle cream, yellow or beige undertone, rather than a cool blue tint. On walls, it tends to feel softer and less stark while still looking white—not obviously yellow.\n\nIts appearance changes with daylight and bulbs, so it’s worth testing a paint sample in the room before choosing.", "conversationId": "518686e01a274636ba4bcea8302b909e"}
